648:   - Display user-friendly error message\n649:   - Log error details\n650: - [ ] Add input validation\n651:   - Validate all user inputs\n652:   - Validate configuration parameters\n653:   - Prevent NaN and infinity\n654: - [ ] Handle edge cases gracefully\n655:   - Empty grid states\n656:   - Zero flux scenarios\n657:   - Invalid level numbers\n658:   - Corrupted localStorage\n659: - [ ] Add retry mechanisms\n660:   - Retry failed operations with exponential backoff\n661:   - Graceful degradation when features fail\n662: - [ ] Handle browser compatibility\n663:   - Check for required APIs (Web Audio, Canvas)\n664:   - Fallbacks for unsupported features\n665:   - Clear error messages\n666: \n667: **Dependencies**: All systems\n668: \n669: ### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n670: - [ ] Implement keyboard navigation\n671:   - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n672:   - Enter/Space to place cells\n673:   - Escape to cancel/close panels\n674:   - Tab navigation through UI controls\n675: - [ ] Add screen reader support\n676:   - ARIA labels for UI elements\n677:   - Announce game state changes\n678:   - Alternative text for visual elements\n679:   - Live regions for score/timer updates\n680: - [ ] Implement reduced motion support\n681:   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n682:   - Disable animations when requested\n683:   - Simplified visual feedback\n684: - [ ] Add high contrast mode\n685:   - Toggle for high contrast colors\n686:   - Larger text option\n687:   - Improved readability\n688: - [ ] Ensure minimum touch targets\n689:   - 44×44px minimum for mobile\n690:   - Spacious clickable areas\n691: - [ ] Focus management\n692:   - Visible focus indicators\n693:   - Logical tab order\n694:   - Focus trap in modals\n695: \n696: **Dependencies**: UI components, user interaction\n697: \n698: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n699: - [ ] Implement performance monitoring\n700:   - FPS counter (development only)\n701:   - Memory usage tracking\n702:   - Component render profiling\n703: - [ ] Add performance optimizations\n704:   - Memoize expensive calculations\n705:   - Virtualize large lists (if applicable)\n706:   - Lazy load non-critical components\n707:   - Debounce/throttle frequent operations\n708: - [ ] Profile and optimize\n709:   - Identify performance bottlenecks\n710:   - Optimize critical paths\n711:   - Ensure 60fps with 500+ cells\n712:   - Test on low-end devices\n713: - [ ] Implement lazy loading\n714:   - Load audio on first interaction\n715:   - Lazy load expert settings panel\n716:   - Code splitting for production\n717: \n718: **Dependencies**: All systems\n719: \n720: ### 6.4 Testing (LOW - Quality Assurance)\n721: - [ ] Set up testing framework\n722:   - Choose testing framework (Vitest recommended)\n723:   - Configure test environment\n724:   - Set up coverage reporting\n725: - [ ] Write unit tests for simulation engine\n726:   - Rule application (born/survive)\n727:   - Toroidal boundaries\n728:   - Age tracking\n729:   - Edge cases (empty grid, static patterns)\n730: - [ ] Write unit tests for phase management\n731:   - Phase transitions\n732:   - Guard conditions\n733:   - Timer accuracy\n734: - [ ] Write unit tests for flux management\n735:   - Placement and refund logic\n736:   - Phase-based behavior\n737: - [ ] Write unit tests for movement detection\n738:   - Connected component detection\n739:   - Centroid tracking\n740:   - Classification accuracy\n741: - [ ] Write unit tests for scoring system\n742:   - Score calculation accuracy\n743:   - Score cap handling\n744:   - High score persistence\n745: - [ ] Write unit tests for level progression\n746:   - Level configuration generation\n747:   - Difficulty scaling\n748: - [ ] Write integration tests\n749:   - End-to-end game flow\n750:   - Level progression\n751:   - Score calculation\n752:   - UI interaction\n753: - [ ] Add manual testing procedures\n754:   - Mobile responsiveness\n755:   - Touch interaction\n756:   - Audio on different browsers\n757:   - Performance with high cell counts\n758:   - Accessibility testing\n759: \n760: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n761: \n762: ### 6.5 Documentation (LOW - Knowledge Transfer)\n763: - [ ] Write README.md\n764:   - Project overview\n765:   - Installation instructions\n766:   - Controls and gameplay guide\n767:   - Configuration options\n768:   - Known issues and limitations\n769: - [ ] Add code comments\n770:   - Complex algorithms (movement detection, simulation)\n771:   - State machine logic\n772:   - Performance-critical sections\n773: - [ ] Document API interfaces\n774:   - Component props\n775:   - Utility functions\n776:   - Configuration schemas\n777:   - Type definitions\n778: - [ ] Create developer guide\n779:   - Architecture overview\n780:   - How to add new features\n781:   - Debugging tips\n782:   - Common patterns\n783: - [ ] Document expert settings\n784:   - Each parameter explanation\n785:   - Recommended values\n786:   - Impact on gameplay\n787: \n788: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n789: \n790: ---\n791: \n792: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n793: \n794: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n795: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n796: \n797: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n798: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n799: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n800: \n801: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n802: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n803: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n804: \n805: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n806: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n807: \n808: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n809: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n810: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n811: \n812: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n813: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n814: \n815: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n816: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n817: \n818: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n819: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n820: \n821: ---\n822: \n823: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n824: \n825: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n826: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n827: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n828: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n829: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n830: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n831: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n832: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n833: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n834: \n835: ## Testing Milestones:\n836: \n837: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n838: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n839: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n840: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n841: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n842: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n843: \n844: ## Success Criteria:\n845: \n846: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n847: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n848: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n849: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n850: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n851: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n852: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n853: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n854: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n855: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n856: - [ ] High score persistence works\n857: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n858: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n859: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n860: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n861: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n862: \n863: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n864: \n865: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n866: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n867: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n868: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n869: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n870: \n871: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n872: \n873: ### Week 1: Foundation\n874: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n875: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n876: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n877: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n878: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n879: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n880: \n881: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n882: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n883: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n884: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n885: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n886: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n887: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n888: \n889: ### Week 3: Scoring & Progression\n890: 13. Movement detection (Day 1-2)\n891: 14. Scoring system (Day 2-3)\n892: 15. Settings panel (Day 3)\n893: 16. Level progression (Day 4)\n894: \n895: ### Week 4: Transitions & Audio\n896: 17. Transition system (Day 1-2)\n897: 18. Victory screen (Day 2)\n898: 19. Audio sonification (Day 3-4)\n899: 20. Visual polish (Day 4)\n900: \n901: ### Week 5: Advanced Features\n902: 21. Expert settings (Day 1-3)\n903: 22. Mobile enhancements (Day 3)\n904: 23. Presets system (Day 4)\n905: \n906: ### Week 6: Quality Assurance\n907: 24. Error handling (Day 1)\n908: 25. Accessibility (Day 1-2)\n909: 26. Performance optimization (Day 2)\n910: 27. Testing (Day 3-4)\n911: 28. Documentation (Day 4)\n912: \n913: ## Notes:\n914: \n915: - Update status (checkmark) as tasks are completed\n916: - The plan is prioritized: CRITICAL first, then HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW\n917: - Parallel tracks enable concurrent work where dependencies allow\n918: - Focus on MVP first, then incrementally add polish\n919: - src/lib/ is the project's standard library for shared utilities\n920: - Prefer consolidated implementations in src/lib/ over ad-hoc copies\n921: - Always run lint and typecheck commands after completing features\n922: - Test on both desktop and mobile throughout development\n923: - Gather user feedback during development to improve UX\n924: - Document decisions and trade-offs in comments or docs\n925: - Keep code modular and maintainable for future enhancements\n926: \n\n(End of file - total 926 lines)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation Plan\n\nThis plan prioritizes building a playable, enjoyable game first, then incrementally enhances with advanced features. All requirements from 14 specification files are included with proper dependencies and priorities.\n\n---\n\n## Sprint 1: Foundation (MVP Core)\n*Goal: Basic Game of Life with visualization, interaction, and game flow*\n\n### 1.1 Project Setup & Build System (CRITICAL - FIRST PRIORITY)\n- [ ] Choose and initialize framework (React/Vite recommended for performance)\n- [ ] Initialize TypeScript project with strict mode\n- [ ] Configure Vite build system\n- [ ] Set up ESLint and Prettier\n- [ ] Create project structure:\n  - src/components/ - React components\n  - src/lib/ - Shared utilities and core logic\n  - src/types/ - TypeScript type definitions\n  - src/hooks/ - Custom React hooks\n  - src/styles/ - CSS/styling","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771163436672,"end":1771163436681}}}}
