- **Spec**: START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- **Spec**: No input during COUNTDOWN phase\n- **Spec**: Prevent START button spam\n- **Old Plan**: Briefly mentioned, now fully specified\n\n### 7. Browser Tab Handling\n- **Spec**: During transitions, pause timer to prevent unseen level advances\n- **Spec**: During gameplay, timer continues when tab inactive\n- **Old Plan**: Not mentioned at all\n- **Impact**: MEDIUM - Prevents unexpected behavior\n\n---\n\n## Missing Features from Specs\n\n### High Priority\n1. Cell preview ghost outline (hover feedback)\n2. Minimum 1 cell rule for START button\n3. High score persistence per level\n4. Skip transition functionality (Space/ESC)\n5. Grid line toggle ('G' key)\n6. Waveform selector dropdown\n7. Flux counter color coding (green/yellow/orange/red)\n\n### Medium Priority\n8. Interaction mode buttons (DRAW/ERASE)\n9. Cursor states (placeable, non-placeable, removable)\n10. Cell animations (fade-in 0.1s, shrink 0.15s)\n11. Phase status display (PLANNING/COUNTDOWN/RUNNING/FINISHED)\n12. Level display UI (\"Level X\")\n13. Pattern breakdown UI (active Movers/Oscillators)\n14. Flux counter animations\n15. Score milestone flash (every 100 points)\n16. Intensity metric (CSS variable)\n17. Expert settings persistence (localStorage)\n18. Expert settings export/import (JSON)\n\n### Low Priority\n19. Touch ripple effect (mobile)\n20. Reduced motion support (accessibility)\n21. High contrast mode (accessibility)\n22. Keyboard navigation (arrow keys, Enter/Space)\n23. Screen reader support (ARIA labels)\n24. Performance monitoring (FPS counter)\n25. Presets (Easy/Normal/Hard/Chaos)\n26. Danger zone (extreme settings with warnings)\n27. Tooltips for expert settings\n\n---\n\n## Key Improvements in New Plan\n\n### Sprint 1 (Foundation)\n- Added COUNTDOWN phase as separate task (was just UI)\n- Added browser tab handling\n- Added grid size buttons (Small/Medium/Large)\n- Added touch-action: none for mobile\n- Added minimum 1 cell rule validation\n\n### Sprint 2 (Core Game Mechanics & UI)\n- NEW: Intro overlay as HIGH priority (first impression)\n- NEW: Main UI controls with glass HUD\n- NEW: UIToggleButton for UI visibility\n- NEW: Phase status display\n- NEW: High score persistence\n- EXPANDED: Settings panel with grid size buttons\n\n### Sprint 3 (Level Progression & Transitions)\n- NEW: Full transition state machine (5 states)\n- NEW: Skip transition functionality\n- NEW: Transition audio (whoosh, complete, start)\n- NEW: Browser tab handling during transitions\n- NEW: Victory screen with total score and replay options\n- EXPANDED: Level progression with all transition phases\n\n### Sprint 4 (Audio & Polish)\n- NEW: Simulation start sound\n- NEW: Level complete/start sounds\n- NEW: Transition whoosh sound\n- NEW: Cell animations (fade-in, shrink)\n- NEW: Cell preview ghost outline\n- NEW: Score milestone flash\n- NEW: Flux counter color coding\n- NEW: Touch ripple effect\n- NEW: Triple-tap gesture for mobile expert settings\n\n### Sprint 5 (Expert Settings)\n- EXPANDED: All expert settings from spec\n- NEW: Presets system (Easy/Normal/Hard/Chaos)\n- NEW: Custom preset support\n- NEW: Tooltips for each parameter\n- NEW: Danger zone with warnings\n- NEW: Export/Import JSON\n\n### Sprint 6 (Quality Assurance)\n- NEW: Accessibility features (keyboard nav, screen reader, reduced motion, high contrast)\n- NEW: Performance monitoring and optimization\n- NEW: Comprehensive testing plan\n- NEW: Documentation (README, code comments, developer guide)\n\n---\n\n## Priority Reordering\n\n### Changed from MEDIUM → CRITICAL\n1. COUNTDOWN phase implementation (was just UI)\n\n### Changed from MEDIUM/LOW → HIGH\n2. Intro overlay (first impression matters)\n3. Transition state machine (critical for game flow)\n4. Skip transition functionality\n5. Grid size buttons\n6. High score persistence\n\n### Changed from not present → MEDIUM\n7. Accessibility features\n8. Cell preview ghost outline\n9. Cursor state m