ment phase status display\n18. Implement settings panel\n19. **Milestone**: Full game UI\n\n---\n\n## Key Recommendations\n\n1. **Start with COUNTDOWN phase** - Don't treat it as just UI, it's a critical game state\n2. **Implement transition system early** - It's not just polish, it's essential for game flow\n3. **Intro overlay should be HIGH priority** - First impression matters for player engagement\n4. **Add accessibility from the start** - It's easier to build in than add later\n5. **Test on mobile throughout** - Don't leave mobile for the end\n6. **Implement all sound effects** - Audio feedback significantly enhances experience\n7. **Add high score persistence** - Gives players long-term goals\n8. **Use expert settings for balancing** - Tune parameters during development\n\n---\n\n## Files Created\n\n1. **IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md** - Comprehensive updated plan with all 6 sprints\n2. **ANALYSIS_SUMMARY.md** - This file, executive summary of findings\n\n---\n\n## Statistics\n\n- **Spec files analyzed**: 14\n- **Implementation items**: ~250 (up from ~106)\n- **Critical gaps identified**: 7\n- **Missing features**: 27\n- **Sprints**: 6 (down from 3, but more detailed)\n- **Estimated timeline**: 6 weeks\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Review updated implementation plan (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)\n2. Start with Sprint 1, Task 1.1 (Project Setup)\n3. Follow recommended implementation order\n4. Update task status (checkmark) as you complete each item\n5. Run lint and typecheck after each feature\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] Week 1: Playable MVP with all phases\n- [ ] Week 2: Full UI and controls\n- [ ] Week 3: Scoring and level progression\n- [ ] Week 4: Complete game loop with audio and transitions\n- [ ] Week 5: Expert settings and mobile support\n- [ ] Week 6: Production-ready with tests and documentation\n- [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n- [ ] Works on desktop and mobile\n- [ ] All features from 14 specs implemented\n- [ ] No critical bugs or edge cases